<title>USA: Lockheed Martin says budget includes F-16s.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin says budget includes F-16s.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp said Tuesday the 1997 defense budget signed into law by President Clinton this week includes $154.9 million for six U.S. Air Force F-16 aircraft.</p>
<p>Lockheed Martin said it would conduct about 45 percent of the work needed in the contract, while other suppliers, which it did not identify, will make up the rest.</p>
<p>The company said it did not immediately know how much the contract would be worth.</p>
<p>The newly funded Block 50/52 F-16 C/D aircraft are to be delivered beginning in 2000.</p>
</text>
